Parse: a BAML function calls the OpenAI API to turn a request like “3 sample orders shipping UPS ground to the US” into typed parameters: order count, carrier, country, order type, and line and quantity limits.

Extract: those parameters build a PostgreSQL query that pulls the matching historical orders.

Analyze: pandas turns that history into frequency tables and conditional probabilities (how often each value appears and which values tend to appear together), plus a distribution of lines per order.

